{"id": "EUVD-2026-103333", "enisaUuid": "b0d2ab77-0cd8-3e6c-8fde-8b460944f59e", "description": "phpMyFAQ from 4.2.0-alpha.2 before 4.2.0-beta lacks brute-force lockout in the removeTwofactorConfig() 2FA removal endpoint, allowing authenticated attackers to guess TOTP codes without limit. Attackers holding a hijacked session and CSRF token can repeatedly POST guesses to /api/user/remove-twofactor to permanently disable the victim's 2FA.", "datePublished": "2026-10-17T18:46:11", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-18T13:25:20", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/thorsten/phpMyFAQ/security/advisories/GHSA-7pjw-6v4g-f837", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/phpmyfaq-4.2.0-alpha.2-before-4.2.0-beta-2fa-brute-force-via-remove-twofactor-endpoint"], "aliases": ["GHSA-9p2j-4h8p-3832", "CVE-2026-111886"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "fe1d082c-6e15-3cb8-9d9a-5f478190a3fe", "product": {"name": "phpMyFAQ", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}, "product_version": "4.2.0-alpha.2 <4.2.0-beta"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "97753052-33e9-39ad-9477-69fbadc68709", "vendor": {"name": "thorsten"}}], "isExploited": false}